Minimal LCAO rt-TDDFT regression for a sub-roundoff displacement at a periodic boundary.

Two H atoms, one non-Gamma k point, two MD steps, and no external field.
The molecule lies parallel to z on the x=0 boundary of a 15-Bohr cube.
Only the first atom can move, along x; its initial velocity is -1e-16 a.u.
The 0.05-fs step gives a fractional displacement of about -1.38e-17.
The transverse force is zero by symmetry, so this deterministic velocity
sets the displacement sign without relying on force roundoff or a user structure.

On unmodified beta11, x-floor(x) rounds this negative coordinate to exactly
1.0. MDCell then passes an inconsistent cell image to rt-TDDFT without the
matching boundary_shift phase correction. The second electronic step loses
continuity despite the negligible physical motion.

With the coordinate fix, x is canonicalized to 0.0 and step 2 converges in
one iteration. The eight-iteration SCF budget is sufficient for the initial
ground state (seven iterations in the verified CPU runs), while beta11 step 2
reaches the limit without converging. With a larger budget beta11 needs ten
iterations and has a spurious energy jump of roughly 79 eV.

The normal Autotest.sh energy checks are supplemented by md_scf.ref:
  MD step, electronic iteration count, number of converged electronic solves
  2        1                           1
The opt-in collector also requires the initial SCF to converge. The initial
SCF iteration count is deliberately not compared across numerical backends.

From tests/05_rtTDDFT:
  OMP_NUM_THREADS=1 MKL_NUM_THREADS=1 bash ../integrate/Autotest.sh \
    -a /absolute/path/to/abacus_std_para -n 4 -o 1 -j 1 \
    -r '^29_NO_MD_boundary_shift$'

The case is registered in CASES_CPU.txt. CPU runs with one and four MPI ranks
were verified; it is not registered for GPU runs.
